  "decision": "go",
  "decision_note": "GO, decided 2026-09-07 by Simon after B6 completed the LLM arm, which is when this gate was pre-registered to be decided. The criterion is that AT LEAST ONE component meaningfully clears the reproduced baseline, and two subtasks answer it with sound same-machine deltas: c2a llm_llammlein 85.95 against a reproduced E1 of 57.40 = +28.55 pp, and dbo llm_llammlein 58.29 against 48.90 = +9.39 pp, both Linux/x86_64 on both sides with delta_blocked false. The fine-tuned LLM RANKS first on all three subtasks and also carries the highest minority-class F1 on all three (dbo subversive 0.4048, vio 0.7226, c2a 0.7462), which is the robustness-relevant half of SQ1 rather than the accuracy half. SECOND CAVEAT ADDED 2026-09-07 BY THE PRE-WRITING AUDIT: that minority-class sentence is a RANK, it had no interval behind it, and D1's pre-registered reporting tiers already said what may be claimed about a class that size. Tested now on the same paired resamples at B=10000 (results/significance.json, every pair carries a `minority_class` block with its tier and gate): on c2a the class holds 659 instances, tier `interpret`, and the LLM's +4.64 pp over the encoder has a paired CI of [-0.0726, -0.0212] -- the directional claim STANDS. On vio, 564 instances, tier `interpret`, the CI is [-0.0617, +0.0002] and it does NOT. On dbo the class holds 60 instances, falls in tier `ci_gated` whose pre-registered rule is 'directional claim only where the CIs do not overlap', the intervals overlap heavily (paired CI [-0.1758, +0.1257]), and `tml_svm` sits BETWEEN the two components being compared at 0.3846 against the encoder's 0.3810 -- so no directional claim is permitted there at all, and the LLM > encoder > TML ordering does not hold on the class SQ1 is about. THE DEFENSIBLE FORM OF THE SENTENCE: the fine-tuned LLM ranks first on the minority class on all three subtasks and is distinguishably better than the encoder on ONE of them (c2a). This mirrors the macro-F1 correction made earlier the same day exactly -- that one was applied to the sentence that was questioned, not to the sentence's shape, and this is the second instance of the same shape. None of it touches the gate, whose criterion is the reproduced BASELINE. CAVEAT ADDED 2026-09-07 AFTER THE SIGNIFICANCE LAYER WAS RE-RUN WITH THE LLM ARM PRESENT: ranking first is not the same as beating, and only the c2a margin over the encoder is distinguishable (McNemar p=0.0018, paired bootstrap CI of the difference excludes zero). On dbo (p=0.066) and vio (p=0.152) the two are INDISTINGUISHABLE by the pre-registered interval rule and by the stronger paired test alike, so #58(b)'s wording rule binds: the text must say indistinguishable and must not crown the maximum. None of this touches the gate itself, whose criterion is clearing the reproduced BASELINE, where the margins are +28.55 pp and +9.39 pp. THREE CAVEATS TRAVEL WITH THIS DECISION AND MUST NOT BE DROPPED WHERE THE NUMBER IS QUOTED. (1) The deltas are indicative, not like-for-like: E2 pools out-of-fold predictions over the whole training split while E1 measured a single 80/20 holdout, and the organiser figures are on a gold test set we do not have. (2) vio has NO reproduced E1 baseline, so its delta stays blocked -- the gate is met without it, on the criterion as written, but vio is not evidence for it until B14/E1b runs. (3) dbo is not comparable on equal terms until E4a, because the organiser DBO baseline uses balanced class weights and this is the D4 reference cell with no imbalance handling at all. Closing this gate is the pre-registered trigger for D8 (Dimension-2 selection by mean rank across E2), which is now unblocked because no arm is missing.",
